{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalAction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalAction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.variational_transport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.variational_transport","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action.lean#L107-L118","doc":"**Categorical transport equation**, as a predicate on the action data:\nthe state is critical iff the covariant derivative `D_∇ ψ = 0`, i.e. the\nmatter term factors through the unit — `ca.matter = fh.unit ≫ fh.counit`.\nNamed (§3b), not asserted: the previous\n`(h_critical : P) : P := h_critical` was self-assuming and stated\nnothing about the action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.variational_yang_mills","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.variational_yang_mills","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action.lean#L96-L105","doc":"**Categorical Yang–Mills equation**: the gauge term is critical iff\n`∇ ★_q F + q[F, ★_q F] = J_ψ`.\nEncoded: at a critical point, the gauge term determines the state. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.variational_einstein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.variational_einstein","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action.lean#L85-L94","doc":"**Categorical Einstein equation**: the gravity term is critical iff\nthe Frobenius–Ricci scalar `R_λ` satisfies `R_λ - ½ tr(R_λ) id = T_q`.\nEncoded: the gravity and matter terms are balanced. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalAction.matter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalAction.matter","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action.lean#L72-L72","doc":"**Matter term**: `λ(ψ* · D_∇ ψ)`, the q-Dirac action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalAction.gauge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalAction.gauge","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action.lean#L70-L70","doc":"**Gauge term**: `λ ∘ tr_A(F_∇ ∧_q ⋆_q F_∇)`, the q-Yang–Mills action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalAction.gravity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalAction.gravity","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action.lean#L68-L68","doc":"**Gravity term**: `tr(q · R_λ)`, the Frobenius–Ricci scalar. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalAction.state","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalAction.state","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action.lean#L66-L66","doc":"The state morphism `ψ : 𝟙 → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalAction.connection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalAction.connection","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action.lean#L64-L64","doc":"The connection on `A` (Definition `def:categorical-connection`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalAction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalAction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalAction","kind":"structure","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action.lean#L47-L72","doc":"**Categorical action functional** `S_q[∇, λ, ψ]`.\n\nThe `R`-valued functional on a quantum observable universe equipped with\nconnection `∇`, Frobenius form `λ`, and state `ψ : 𝟙 → A`:\n\n```\nS_q = tr(q · R_λ)          (gravity)\n    + λ ∘ tr_A(F_∇ ∧_q ⋆_q F_∇)  (gauge)\n    + λ(ψ* · D_∇ ψ)        (matter)\n```\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:categorical-action}`\nRef: [kock2004] ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:categorical-action","label":"def:categorical-action","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalConnection.leibniz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalConnection.leibniz","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action.lean#L45-L45","doc":"**Leibniz rule**: `∇ ∘ μ = leibniz_rhs`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalConnection.leibniz_rhs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalConnection.leibniz_rhs","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action.lean#L43-L43","doc":"The Leibniz rule RHS. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalConnection.nabla","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalConnection.nabla","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action.lean#L41-L41","doc":"The connection morphism `∇ : A → A ⊗ Ω¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalConnection.Omega1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalConnection.Omega1","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action.lean#L39-L39","doc":"The object of 1-forms `Ω¹` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalConnection.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalConnection.mk","kind":"ctor","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalConnection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalConnection","kind":"structure","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action.lean#L33-L45","doc":"**Categorical connection** on a Frobenius–Hopf object.\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:categorical-connection}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:categorical-connection","label":"def:categorical-connection","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-connection.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}